Yes — there are two compounding problems here.

**1. `MediaViewerModalContent`'s FlatList has no windowing config**, so on open it instantiates a wide window of pages (RN default `windowSize` is 21). Each `MediaImagePage` mounts immediately fires `resolveEncryptedImage` in its `useEffect`, so you see all of them "rendering."

**2. `renderItem` is recreated whenever `currentIndex` changes** ([MediaViewerModalContent.tsx:208](src/shared/components/media-viewer-modal/MediaViewerModalContent.tsx#L208)), which forces FlatList to re-run `renderItem` for every cached cell on every swipe. Combined with the fact that `getImageContent(event)` ([MediaImagePage.tsx:27](src/shared/components/media-viewer-modal/MediaImagePage.tsx#L27)) returns a fresh reference each render → `load` callback identity changes → the decrypt `useEffect` re-fires.

The fix is two-part:

**A. Limit the FlatList window** ([MediaViewerModalContent.tsx:243-254](src/shared/components/media-viewer-modal/MediaViewerModalContent.tsx#L243-L254)):

```jsx
<FlatList
  data={pages}
  renderItem={renderItem}
  keyExtractor={keyExtractor}
  getItemLayout={getItemLayout}
  horizontal
  inverted={payload.source === "timeline"}
  pagingEnabled
  showsHorizontalScrollIndicator={false}
  initialScrollIndex={initialPageIndex}
  onViewableItemsChanged={handleViewableItemsChanged}
  initialNumToRender={1}
  maxToRenderPerBatch={1}
  windowSize={3}          // current + 1 each side
  removeClippedSubviews
/>
```

**B. Stop tying `renderItem` to `currentIndex`.** Right now passing `isActive={index === currentIndex}` to the video page is what couples them. Two options:

- Move `isActive` detection into `MediaVideoPage` itself by reading the current index from a ref or a small jotai atom, so `renderItem` only depends on stable callbacks.
- Or wrap `MediaImagePage`/`MediaVideoPage` in `React.memo` and pull `isActive` via context. `React.memo` on the pages alone (with stable `event`/`onSingleTap`/`onLocalUriChange`) will already block most of the re-render churn — but only after you stop recreating `renderItem` on every index change, since otherwise the component identity used in cells stays the same but the props lambda (`onUriChange`) is fresh each pass.

While you're there, also stabilize the decrypt effect in [MediaImagePage.tsx:32-54](src/shared/components/media-viewer-modal/MediaImagePage.tsx#L32-L54): key `load` on the event id rather than the `content` object, e.g. `useMemo(() => getImageContent(event), [getEventId(event)])`. That prevents the decrypt from re-firing when the parent re-renders for unrelated reasons.

Want me to apply these changes?

